From 98ca6e0d72ca24d4991dfc80c9e098fd1de9af03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:11:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app): generator defect fixes make cached toolpaths
 stale

A project saved before PR #3684 kept the old cached toolpath of a tabbed
outside 2D Contour and posted it while reading as current: the stamp's
written rule asked for a new salt only when a verify law changes (#3704).

The rule decided (option 1, the lean one): a change of generator output
that fixes a defect makes old caches stale. It lives at the salt as the
named constant GENERATOR_OUTPUT_VERSION, written into every operation
stamp. The PR that changes what a generator emits bumps it in the same
PR; a byte-identical refactor does not. The rule text is in the stamp
comment and in docs/decisions/3704-generator-output-version.md.

The term moves every stamp once (the churn the salt bumps produce): the
committed catalog caches are regenerated (no .nc golden moved), and the
re-pinned stamp constants of deburr_cache_stamp and wire_stamp are
re-captured, the same re-pin the v3/v4 salt bumps did.

Pins (crates/app/src/operation/stamp_tests.rs):
- a_bump_of_the_generator_output_version_moves_the_stamp
- an_unchanged_generator_output_version_keeps_a_saved_cache_current
- a_tabbed_contour_saved_before_the_bump_reads_stale (the catalog
  contour-tabs case: a stamp rewritten to the pre-bump value reads
  Stale on load, the general stale reason, and never posts)

Gate: camcraft-app --lib (321 passed), the touched integration suites
(example_catalog*, plunge_depth_tab, tool_after_state, stale_rapid_law,
tilt_basis_compat, wire_stamp, deburr_cache_stamp, contour_start_point,
conformance, first_part_programs, mcp_verify), cargo xtask catalog
--check, clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings: all green.

Fixes #3704
